1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,440
Angie, where are you?

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,200
Sylvia, answer me!

3
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:16,040
(five months later)

4
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:45,200
The client is chasing me for the revision.

5
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:47,240
What revisions?

6
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,480
Go change! I'll figure out how to respond.

7
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,720
I want to stay and watch the stars tonight.

8
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,400
When is the sunset?

9
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,360
6:30 p.m., we must wait.

10
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:02,080
You're right. Can't rush it.

11
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,720
Whatever should happen will happen.

12
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,280
(Mom)

13
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,600
What will you be home today?

14
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:21,200
You went camping for a few days

15
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,880
and didn't even text me.

16
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,120
I'm worried about you.

17
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,600
You were never this irresponsible.

18
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,160
What is it?

19
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:36,560
You can see the Venus Conjunction tonight.

20
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:39,040
What does it mean?

21
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,880
It's a bad omen.

22
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,760
In ancient China, it's called
Taibai entering the Moon,

23
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,600
it usually means war.

24
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,160
That's dangerous. We should take shelter.

25
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,760
Let's go home.

26
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,320
No need. In the western world,

27
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:57,520
Venus and the Moon are related to love.

28
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,440
It's a romantic celestial phenomenon.

29
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:05,000
You're just saying that to make me stay.

30
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,440
I'm saying I want to stay and watch,

31
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:09,600
but you're free to go.

32
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:11,920
But I want to watch with you

33
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:15,600
what war and romance are about.

34
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,400
Mom, I'm not coming home tonight.

35
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:23,920
Your son is fine, don't worry.

36
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:26,400
What's special about the Venus Conjunction

37
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:30,720
is the location where they'll meet.

38
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,440
Tell me, mighty one...

39
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:36,480
what's the meaning of the Venus Conjunction
for a Scorpion?

40
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,320
In astrology,

41
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:41,760
the Moon affects how people handle
their feelings.

42
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:45,280
Venus is a symbol of love.

43
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:51,040
Scorpio seeks the ultimate romance in love.

44
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:57,040
The Venus Conjunction should mean
unforgettable love.

45
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:01,520
Unforgettable love?

46
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:04,560
Should we pledge our undying love?

47
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:09,880
I remember you're not big on promises.

48
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,680
That's why I didn't promise
not to make a promise.

49
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:20,400
Unforgettable doesn't mean a pledge
of undying love.

50
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:23,280
Like a moth to a flame,

51
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,520
that's the ultimate romance.

52
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,720
Knowing it will burn to death,

53
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:32,480
it's still swarm towards it.

54
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:07,360
Looks like you figured it out.

55
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,360
The Venus Conjunction?

56
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:14,520
The owner doesn't want paintings
or decorations on the wall.

57
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:17,360
But the wife doesn't want to leave it empty.

58
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:19,400
Now I put in a lamp

59
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:21,960
with the effect of a halo of
the Venus Conjunction.

60
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:25,040
They can also change the color
depending on the mood.

61
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:29,400
See? Your inspiration is always nearby.

62
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:32,640
But the pace in Hong Kong is too fast.

63
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:35,400
We only see what's in front of us

64
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,760
and overlook what's around us.

65
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,840
I did not.

66
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,320
My Muse is right next to me.

67
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,760
I'll wash these.

68
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:53,200
Then I'm off to a client meeting.

69
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,480
My Mom's birthday is coming up.

70
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,400
We'll have dinner with her and
you can meet her.

71
00:05:58,520 --> 00:05:59,560
We'll see.

72
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,080
I take that as a yes.

73
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,840
(Mom)

74
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:15,920
Auntie?

75
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,600
You must be Sylvia!

76
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,720
Why did you answer the phone?

77
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:20,000
Where's my son?

78
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,400
Is it something urgent?

79
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:24,960
He didn't come home because of you?

80
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,600
We stayed one more night to watch the stars.

81
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,360
He should have told me.

82
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,520
He's getting irresponsible as he gets older.

83
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,360
Auntie, you said so he's a grown man.

84
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,200
Don't worry. I'll tell him to call you.

85
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:38,320
Hello? She cut me off!?

86
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:42,400
Who is she? She's so rude.

87
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:47,840
Are you done?

88
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:50,960
You're checking my phone?

89
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,840
No, your Mom is tracking you down.

90
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,520
Mom? What does she want?

91
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,760
She said you didn't tell her you
won't be home.

92
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:59,200
You better call her back.

93
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:02,000
What? I already told her.

94
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:06,000
Oops, the message didn't go out.

95
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:09,920
I'm home!

96
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:14,480
Mom? Mom?

97
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:21,520
"No need to find me."

98
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:24,400
Two bamboos.

99
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,360
Pong!

100
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:27,960
Here he is.

101
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,200
Auntie Ching.

102
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,640
Auntie Bing! Auntie Fung!

103
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:36,880
What a great hand...Mom!

104
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,360
I told you not to look for me.

105
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:43,360
But I missed you. Since you weren't home,

106
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,120
I called Auntie Ching to see if you're here.

107
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,800
I know playing mahjong can be tiring,

108
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:49,200
I brought you Shanghai dishes as a treat.

109
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,640
I'll heat them up for you.

110
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:53,840
Don't mess up the kitchen.

111
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,360
You have such a sweet tongue,

112
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,760
but you tend to disappear once you go out.

113
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,840
Lan is worried about you.

114
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:01,440
It was my fault.

115
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:04,320
I actually sent a message telling you
I won't be home.

116
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,040
But the reception was poor where I was

117
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,200
and I didn't check to make sure it was sent.

118
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:11,440
It was bad of me to make her worry.

119
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,480
Lan, don't be mad anymore.

120
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,720
What's wrong with you?

121
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:20,160
He brings food and you change your tune?

122
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,520
Enjoy your game.

123
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:24,400
I'll heat this up for you.

124
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,000
Have some tea, Mom.

125
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:34,400
OK, you're forgiven since you coaxed me.

126
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:39,120
But I seriously doubt your taste.

127
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:43,440
Your girlfriend was rude and hung up on me.

128
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:46,560
She's just very straightforward.

129
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,120
She's not a bad person.

130
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:51,680
She knows about feng shui and divination.

131
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,120
You two should hit it off.

132
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:56,480
You better give me her name and birthday.

133
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,240
I want to see if you two are compatible.

134
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:03,200
Siu Zi-yiu, November 11, 1998.

135
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,040
Just the date? What time?

136
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,640
I'll ask.

137
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:09,360
Your girlfriend must be a witch.

138
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:11,920
She used black magic to get a hold on you.

139
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:15,760
No, you have a hold on my heart.

140
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,360
I treat you very well.

141
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:20,080
I booked a table for your birthday.

142
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:22,560
I invited Sylvia to celebrate with you.

143
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:25,280
You'll love her when you meet her.

144
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,200
Try not to be so subjective, OK?

145
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:30,480
I will get her birth data myself.

146
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:33,440
OK, whatever you want.

147
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:40,560
I, Man Nga-kei, born March 15, 1996,

148
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,480
do solemnly ask for a good marriage...
Hey!

149
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,080
Aren't you praying for yourself?

150
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:46,160
I did that last month.

151
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,840
Since you're here with me

152
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,240
and won't take the initiative,
I'll have to do it on your behalf.

153
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:52,240
Where else can you find a bestie like me?

154
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:56,560
May the Lover's Rock help Man Nga-kei
find a good catch,

155
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:59,440
someone handsome, funny and rich.

156
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,480
But most, most, most importantly,
someone who loves her only.

157
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,720
You must kowtow too. Come on!

158
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:08,160
1...2...3...

159
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,720
You must touch it.

160
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,920
Throw the wishing placard too.

161
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,560
Wishing placard?

162
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,520
Throw the wishing placard too.

163
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:29,520
Wishing placard?

164
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,760
Yes! In one take.

165
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:36,320
What did you wish for? Why is it so hard?

166
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,760
No...don't look!

167
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:39,960
(For Yiu Wai-lan and Yau You-fong's safety)

168
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:40,840
(and all goes well. From : Man Nga-kei)

169
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:43,760
Man Nga-kei, you're still thinking of
that scumbag?

170
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:46,560
We used to be family.

171
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,120
I'm just praying for their safety.

172
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:53,280
Yau You-fong is safe because of you,
not Heaven.

173
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,440
You risked your life to save him

174
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,520
but he's now with that witch.

175
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:59,040
He thinks she saved his life.

176
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,040
And you? He didn't even thank you.

177
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,080
He sent his regards at the hospital.

178
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,920
I wasn't hurt.

179
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,640
I didn't tell him I pulled him up.

180
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,640
Why didn't you?

181
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:14,080
He only has eyes for Sylvia.

182
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,680
If I told him,

183
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:17,760
someone would think I'm fighting for him.

184
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:20,560
Even the tree won't bless the scumbag.

185
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:22,080
How could you still defend him?

186
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:25,920
Stop calling him a scumbag.

187
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,240
We were divorced when he met Sylvia.

188
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,640
He wasn't a two-timer or a scumbag.

189
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:34,280
OK...he's not a scumbag. But you're lovesick

190
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,560
and can't let go but act indifferent.

191
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:39,920
Liz, I know you care about me,

192
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,280
but I really need a bit more time...

193
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,360
Your flat is full of his paintings

194
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:47,800
and you're still making payments
with him on the flat.

195
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:50,080
It'll take forever to get over him.

196
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,640
Why don't you sell the flat,

197
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,800
get your money back and cut yourself loose?

198
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,280
No, the property market is in a slump.

199
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,040
I don't want to cut losses right now.

200
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,200
You're driving me crazy.

201
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,120
Yes!

202
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,920
Look, Liz! The tree changed its mind.

203
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:18,560
Are you done? Can we go now?

204
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,640
(Man Nga-kei)

205
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:42,080
Chris, has it been ten years since
we last saw each other?

206
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,600
Probably.

207
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:46,880
You were quite earnest in high school.

208
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,480
I thought you were a bookworm.

209
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:51,200
But now, you're tall and handsome

210
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:54,160
just like an oppa. Right, Angie?

211
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:57,520
Angie, Liz said you're a copywriter
at a TV station

212
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:58,800
and you know just about everything.

213
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:01,600
I'd like to talk to you more.

214
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:06,240
I only did the research when
I had a show to do.

215
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:09,120
I only know a little bit...

216
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:13,440
I heard you're quite a gourmet,

217
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,880
let's order some food.

218
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,480
Angie, what would you like?

219
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,920
Whatever. I'll let you decide.

220
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:22,160
Mom, happy birthday.

221
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:25,120
Here's to your good health.

222
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,720
Most importantly, to your beauty.

223
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,760
Good boy!

224
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:31,760
Sylvia and I bought you a present.

225
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:34,000
Auntie, happy birthday.

226
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,440
Open it and take a look.

227
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,440
Thank you.

228
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,000
It's beautiful.

229
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:44,240
I know nothing about jade.

230
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,680
Sylvia picked it out.

231
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,920
Here. I'll put it on for you.

232
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:47,840
Great!

233
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:56,160
You did a show on local ruins?

234
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,960
I like to watch urban exploration
when I was abroad.

235
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:02,720
Anything special about the local ruins?

236
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:06,880
It's much easier to find them in Hong Kong.

237
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:09,120
Because in the US or Europe...

238
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,640
Auntie!

239
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,480
Angie!

240
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:19,680
Happy birthday, here's to your good health.

241
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:23,360
Thank you...

242
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,680
Cantonese opera classics?

243
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:29,920
How did you manage to find them?

244
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:32,080
I hope you like them.

245
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,720
A colleague in the music department
was selling them.

246
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,200
Then they must be expensive.

247
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:40,000
You're so sweet,

248
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:43,280
but your memory is getting worse.

249
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:46,800
No, I saw you having dinner with

250
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:49,440
Davis and his girlfriend last night
in a restaurant.

251
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:50,920
I just didn't want to intrude.

252
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:52,720
You were there?

253
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:55,760
Dinner was unbearable.

254
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,000
Why did you start playing the stock market?

255
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,440
Sylvia taught you?

256
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,600
Auntie, are you interested?

257
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,280
I can get you some information.

258
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:07,440
No need. My son and I don't have
any luck with making quick money.

259
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:12,520
Nothing can help our luck.

260
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:15,000
Whether one knows how to invest,

261
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:18,800
cannot be summed up by just saying
you don't have luck with quick money.

262
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:21,680
After my son met this witch,

263
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:24,000
he's definitely out of luck.

264
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,280
Thanks.

265
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:41,440
The Boss wants to know what you're doing.

266
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:42,480
Did you finish the sketch?

267
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,920
Where are you?

268
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,840
Call him back.

269
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,840
Last time, you didn't show up
and the client was pissed.

270
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,600
I'm not surprised he doesn't like
your design.

271
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:56,480
In our business, the client must come first.

272
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,880
If you don't understand, you should quit.

273
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:10,160
If you wish to invest in real estate,

274
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:13,280
I think you should pick the East.

275
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,320
I drew the Three of Wands.

276
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:17,080
Is my destiny overseas?

277
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,120
It favors overseas development.

278
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:23,360
Investing in real estate in SE Asia
is the right thing to do.

279
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:26,000
Why SE Asia? What does it stand for?

280
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:28,240
That doesn't matter.

281
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:30,560
Investment is about ROI, rate of return.

282
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:34,200
Rent in SE Asia is about 4% to 6%,

283
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,320
which is higher than Hong Kong.

284
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:37,520
You're an investor too?

285
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:41,040
Of course. Why would I miss out
on a good thing?

286
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:48,280
Is overseas investment suitable for me?

287
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,160
Yes,

288
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:53,160
but I thought you're not
interested in investments.

289
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,200
I thought it's just a game for you.

290
00:16:56,320 --> 00:17:01,440
I used to think it was great I can
make money doing something I like.

291
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,240
Now I prefer to make money.

292
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:05,200
If the clients don't appreciate my work,

293
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:09,040
why waste my time and effort on them?

294
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:12,360
Why? More changes on your design?

295
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:14,880
Not to mention the games
the Boss is playing.

296
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:18,960
I did everything the client wanted
and changed the design.

297
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,360
But the Boss kept saying the client
still didn't like it

298
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:22,760
and wanted me to start from scratch.

299
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,960
He obviously wanted me to quit.

300
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,720
Don't be mad.

301
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:30,720
You're angry because I gave you the idea.

302
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:33,120
They don't appreciate a good idea.

303
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:37,600
I didn't realize I mean so much to you.

304
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,680
I should have followed your lead to invest.

305
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:47,120
Then I don't need to work for anyone
and take crap from them.

306
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:50,000
Every decision has a cause and effect.

307
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,680
If you were not in design,

308
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:54,520
you wouldn't have taken on the
renovation of S Bar.

309
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:58,240
If you never went to S Bar,
we wouldn't have met.

310
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:59,920
Now that we have met,

311
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:03,920
should I follow your lead to invest?

312
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:09,120
Whether you invest your money in
real estate or your love in me,

313
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:11,040
there are risks involved.

314
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:14,640
Sometimes, you need guts to make money.

315
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:17,840
Some people are more suitable
to work for someone else.

316
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:20,160
There. I exposed you as a quack.

317
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:22,480
It's in your fate.

318
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:25,760
But it still depends on if you have
the smarts for it

319
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,440
and how you go by doing it.

320
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:32,360
I have done a lot of homework.

321
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,960
It's not a random decision.

322
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:36,800
How hard is the homework?

323
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:41,360
You better start doing it.

324
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,760
Wait up!

325
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:56,160
I might have goaded you a bit,

326
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,160
there's no need to stay up all night.

327
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:00,440
I couldn't stop reading.

328
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,200
I have an initial idea already.

329
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,040
Take a look at these buildings.

330
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:06,880
Thailand?

331
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:09,840
The ROI on these areas is high.

332
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:13,440
But they're quite expensive, my budget...

333
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,280
we can go in on it.

334
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,120
I considered more than the ROI,

335
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,360
but also which areas are suitable for us.

336
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:25,120
These building should be OK for both of us.

337
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:28,640
When we went camping and mentioned
overseas properties,

338
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,000
you sounded like you yearn for it.

339
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:32,720
I guess you want to invest in
overseas property

340
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,760
because you want to live there.

341
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:38,360
Yes, I do...

342
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:41,120
Like me, you don't want to be tied down.

343
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,440
I'm not trying to trap you with a flat.

344
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,920
For such a huge investment,

345
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:48,480
I can only chip in a small share.

346
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:50,880
That's easy. I'll pay for the big share.

347
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,840
If we can sort out the money,

348
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:57,080
this is a good plan.

349
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:02,960
I didn't like to plan ahead,

350
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:06,080
but meeting you gave me more possibilities.

351
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,120
Such as?

352
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:09,920
Such as...getting married and have kids.

353
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:13,120
What about getting married but no kids?

354
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:17,360
Or have kids without getting married.

355
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:24,080
Either way...nothing has to change.

356
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:27,360
As long as we're happy, just like right now.

357
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:31,040
I don't think my fate is right
for this area.

358
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:33,920
Well...I'll do what I do best.

359
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:37,040
I'll go change and get you breakfast.

360
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:08,560
See you at 8:30 p.m. next Monday,
on Overseas Property Guide.

361
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:16,600
You know anything about overseas property?

362
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:18,360
You seem quite interested.

363
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:21,720
Anyone with extra money would check out
overseas property.

364
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:23,880
It's not as expensive as Hong Kong

365
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:25,880
and the ROI is much higher.

366
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:29,040
Just like Thailand, in Bangkok alone,

367
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:30,920
the ROI is around 5% to 6%.

368
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:33,480
Phuket is even higher at 8%.

369
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:35,400
What does that mean? You pay the downpayment

370
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,400
someone else will pay the mortgage for you.

371
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:40,360
You seem to know a lot.
Are you so confident?

372
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:42,680
80% if not 100%.

373
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:45,480
I looked up everything in Thailand.

374
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:48,120
You spent a lot of money on downpayment.

375
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:51,080
Then invested in something else.

376
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:53,080
Do you still have money left?

377
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:57,640
I'm short on my own.

378
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:59,400
But you have.

379
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:02,120
Mom, let's make an investment

380
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,680
and make some money together.

381
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,120
Count me out.

382
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:08,440
I know nothing about overseas property.

383
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:10,600
It's too risky.

384
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:14,800
Besides, all my money is in time deposit.

385
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:16,800
If I withdraw now, there'll be a penalty.

386
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:17,800
No thanks.

387
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:20,480
Mom, you're doing your Maths wrong.

388
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:23,240
If the interest rate of the time deposit
cannot keep up with inflation,

389
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:25,400
you're actually losing money.

390
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:27,600
Owning property is different.

391
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,760
Rent will go up with inflation,

392
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:31,800
you can't lose.

393
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:33,760
Sylvia and I will chip in the money.

394
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:35,880
She already has a broker in Thailand.

395
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:38,360
What? You're partnering with the witch?

396
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:40,480
Don't listen to her.

397
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:43,000
Mom, stop calling her a witch.

398
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:45,520
I read through the information myself.

399
00:22:45,640 --> 00:22:47,160
I formed my own judgment.

400
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:48,680
How long have you known her?

401
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:50,920
She's asking you for money already?

402
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:55,640
Last time I told her we don't have
much luck with making quick money.

403
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:59,000
She already contradicted me.

404
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:00,520
Come to think of it,

405
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:04,360
she already planned to ask you
for money back then.

406
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:06,840
Don't fall for it, son!

407
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:11,320
You don't like her because
she contradicted you.

408
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,240
I have the freedom to choose.

409
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:16,320
You can't stop me from seeing anyone.

410
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:19,400
Forget it. I'll be in my room.

411
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:24,360
Look at you. You were not like this before.

412
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:27,040
You yelled at me because of a witch?

413
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:29,160
I just don't want anyone to swindle you.

414
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:37,960
Angie!

415
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:41,240
What's up? What's so urgent?

416
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:44,560
I need to discuss something with you.

417
00:23:44,680 --> 00:23:47,760
Let's sell the flat and split the money.

418
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:49,320
All of a sudden?

419
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:52,840
We agreed I can stay there

420
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,600
and pay you rent.

421
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:59,160
Yes, it's my fault. I need money.

422
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:00,760
Or we can keep the flat,

423
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,080
you pay me back for the downpayment

424
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:03,480
and I'll surrender the title.

425
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:06,480
Wait! What's the rush?

426
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:09,520
I saw a few properties in Thailand.

427
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:13,720
They're cheap and the ROI is much higher
than Hong Kong.

428
00:24:13,840 --> 00:24:16,520
I don't want to miss the opportunity.

429
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:19,880
I'm chipping in with my girlfriend Sylvia.

430
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:21,640
She already contacted a real estate agent,

431
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,720
I don't want to hold her off.
That's why I need the money.

432
00:24:23,840 --> 00:24:28,080
OK, but you have never invested in anything.

433
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:32,440
Did something happen at work?
You're not happy?

434
00:24:32,560 --> 00:24:34,680
My interest is in design.

435
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:36,560
But I must compromise to make a living.

436
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:40,120
I just want to make my first pot of gold
while I'm still young.

437
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:42,360
There's no room for ideals unless
you have money.

438
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:44,440
I can't miss this opportunity.

439
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:46,080
That makes sense.

440
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:48,600
But why the sudden decision?

441
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:51,400
Which corporation is responsible for
the project?

442
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:52,600
Can it be trusted?

443
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,080
Do you know anything about it?

444
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:56,120
I have done my homework.

445
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:58,840
I studied Bangkok and Phuket

446
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,320
and did all the calculations.

447
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:02,560
Bangkok is a major city,

448
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:04,120
the flat will be rented out to locals.

449
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:05,480
Phuket is different.

450
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:08,040
It's mainly rented out to tourists.

451
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:09,400
Look at the ROI,

452
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:12,080
it's really high and worth investing.

453
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,480
Are you kidding me?

454
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:16,560
What's wrong with you?

455
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,080
Do you really want to buy property?

456
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:20,040
You wrote in your sketch book!

457
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,760
This is your life's work.

458
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:24,560
This is where you put down your ideas.

459
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,480
You're not the Yau You-fong I know.

460
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:27,960
He's not impulsive.

461
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:30,200
You didn't even go out there
and you talk about owning property?

462
00:25:30,280 --> 00:25:31,800
What's wrong with you?

463
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:34,480
You're a designer, remember?

464
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:38,720
You told me a client's content

465
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:41,600
is a designer's greatest satisfaction.

466
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:45,520
Because design is not an interest or a hobby

467
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:47,520
it's a pursuit of ideals.

468
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,280
You didn't even go out there!

469
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:52,240
But you want to buy a flat
based on a leaflet?

470
00:25:56,280 --> 00:25:59,320
OK, you want to buy a flat?

471
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:01,800
You want money?

472
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,760
You can have the flat back.

473
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:07,640
Go buy your new flat.

474
00:26:19,840 --> 00:26:23,880
I can't figure this out. Can you help me?

475
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:26,760
Sure!

476
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,600
You're not the Yau You-fong I know.

477
00:26:30,760 --> 00:26:32,600
He's not impulsive.

478
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:40,800
I signed the power of attorney.

479
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,600
The law firm will send it to you.

480
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:44,480
This is your net worth.

481
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:48,040
Decide for yourself if this is
how you want to invest.

482
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:53,160
Try putting your hand behind you.

483
00:26:53,280 --> 00:26:55,960
Raise your head a little.

484
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:58,680
Done. It's perfect.

485
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:00,040
Really?

486
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,320
You look so handsome.

487
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:03,160
Let me see...

488
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:05,400
You made me look fat.

489
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:07,160
Your painting skill failed.

490
00:27:07,280 --> 00:27:09,880
That's because you're a poor teacher.

491
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:13,800
But you'll have more time to teach me
from now on.

492
00:27:14,120 --> 00:27:17,640
Sylvia, about buying overseas property.

493
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:20,840
I think we should think twice...

494
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:24,360
True. I spoke to the real estate agent.

495
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:27,320
He said the cost-performance ratio
is rather high for these buildings,

496
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:28,680
He bought one for himself.

497
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:31,720
I already confirmed with him verbally.

498
00:27:31,840 --> 00:27:32,840
You did?

499
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,640
Yes, weren't you very keen?

500
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:39,160
Yes, but we haven't actually seen it.

501
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:42,480
People are fighting for quality property
like this.

502
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:45,040
Act on it once you made up your mind

503
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,440
or it'll be gone.

504
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:48,440
Still. We should think it over.

505
00:27:48,560 --> 00:27:50,120
Let's not rush into it.

506
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:52,120
Are you toying with me?

507
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:54,600
When I was thinking, you said it was OK.

508
00:27:54,760 --> 00:27:56,320
Now that I spoke to the agent,

509
00:27:56,440 --> 00:27:58,680
you want to go back on your word.

510
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:03,520
I'm sorry, I was too impulsive.

511
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,280
It's better to calm down.

512
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:09,760
We should spend more time to understand
the overseas market

513
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:12,280
to minimize our risks.

514
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:15,240
You know I'm not good with
long-term investments.

515
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,040
Besides, money is an issue.

516
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:19,160
I don't have enough money for you.

517
00:28:19,320 --> 00:28:22,680
Look, I'm not asking you to give me money,

518
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:24,120
we're both chipping in.

519
00:28:24,280 --> 00:28:25,520
But I don't have enough.

520
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:26,920
I can't ask Mom for money

521
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:29,160
and make her bear the risk.

522
00:28:29,360 --> 00:28:31,560
I also promised to give the flat to my ex.

523
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:32,680
I can't go back on my word.

524
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:36,840
I see. Your mother and ex don't want us

525
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:38,760
to invest or be together.

526
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:41,320
No, they're against making the investment.

527
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:43,840
Why do you need your ex's approval?

528
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,160
What kind of ex is she?

529
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:46,680
There's nothing between us.

530
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:48,080
Nothing?

531
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:51,400
You changed your tune after talking to her.

532
00:28:51,520 --> 00:28:52,920
Does that mean you listen to her

533
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,600
and she's more important? Then what am I?

534
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:56,440
Nothing I say matters, right?

535
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:58,000
Come on, listen to me...

536
00:28:58,120 --> 00:29:00,760
Don't touch me! Go back to your ex!

537
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:02,680
Sylvia!

538
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:09,720
Sylvia!

539
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:12,480
Calm down and let me explain.

540
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,440
What's there to explain?

541
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:17,400
I met with my ex to discuss
selling our flat.

542
00:29:17,560 --> 00:29:19,520
Are you selling?

543
00:29:19,640 --> 00:29:20,920
No, right?

544
00:29:21,080 --> 00:29:22,560
That means you're not over her

545
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:24,480
and you want to dump me for her.

546
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,520
You talked about our future

547
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,840
and how we invest together
and move overseas.

548
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:32,360
That's just talk.
You have not thought about our future.

549
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:34,280
No, Sylvia!

550
00:29:34,880 --> 00:29:37,640
Precisely because I'm thinking about
our future, we must be careful

551
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:40,000
and not put all our eggs in one basket.

552
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:41,480
I don't want any accidents.

553
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:44,800
What accidents?

554
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,960
You think I'm swindling your money?

555
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:48,400
That's not what I mean.

556
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:49,600
Then what do you mean?

557
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:52,360
You had no intention to sell
your flat, right?

558
00:29:52,520 --> 00:29:54,360
Don't bother. Get out!

559
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,640
Are you OK?

560
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:14,360
Let me dress your wound.

561
00:30:14,520 --> 00:30:15,880
Don't bother!

562
00:30:16,640 --> 00:30:20,200
You're a hypocrite! You're lying.

563
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:22,680
No, I'm not. I do love you, Sylvia.

564
00:30:22,760 --> 00:30:24,600
Then sell your flat.

565
00:30:25,520 --> 00:30:27,000
No?

566
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:29,520
Why can't you give me more time to think?

567
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:31,400
Because I think you're lying.

568
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:34,200
All along, you're still in love with her.

569
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:37,720
I have nothing to say to you. Get out!

570
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:38,560
Sylvia...

571
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,360
Out!

572
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:46,120
Calm down! I'll call you.

573
00:30:52,720 --> 00:30:54,840
(several days later)

574
00:30:56,960 --> 00:31:00,440
We'll talk when you get over this.

575
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:02,080
Are you feeling better?

576
00:31:02,200 --> 00:31:04,360
Let's go for dessert buffet.

577
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:09,720
(Sylvia on live)

578
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:25,080
Hello, everyone! I'm in a good mood today.

579
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:28,920
20% off on all orgonite pyramids
and crystal bracelets.

580
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:32,840
She's in the mood to livestream
but not in the mood to call me?

581
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:35,640
Want some fruits?

582
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:39,600
Amethyst can clear your head...

583
00:31:39,680 --> 00:31:40,680
What are you watching?

584
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:42,600
Sylvia's livestreaming.

585
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:45,560
Leave a message if you want them.

586
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:49,640
This quack's crystals are trash.

587
00:31:49,800 --> 00:31:52,040
Exactly! Wearing it is worse than before.

588
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,480
She claims they're consecrated.

589
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:55,160
That's the excuse to jack up the price.

590
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:57,480
She's treating us like suckers.

591
00:31:57,600 --> 00:32:01,160
The effect of crystals depends on the user.

592
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:03,880
If you don't have the right vibe,

593
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,840
the crystal cannot raise the dead.

594
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:09,080
Where did these anti-fans come from?

595
00:32:09,240 --> 00:32:10,520
What are anti-fans?

596
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,680
People who maliciously criticize someone.

597
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:15,160
Don't bother to defend yourself,
you bloody hag!

598
00:32:15,320 --> 00:32:18,480
She's neither Chinese nor western,
neither fish nor fowl.

599
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:20,000
She's nothing but a quack!

600
00:32:20,120 --> 00:32:21,640
She used black magic to steal a guy
from a client.

601
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:25,240
Is that true? That's malicious!

602
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:27,320
You're free to say anything

603
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:29,520
just make sure you have proof.

604
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:31,720
Look! Someone just spilled the beans
and posted a link.

605
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:33,160
See for yourselves.

606
00:32:34,520 --> 00:32:38,560
What are all those contraptions?

607
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:42,000
Those are fakes. It's not true.

608
00:32:42,080 --> 00:32:43,840
Don't believe any of it.

609
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,480
Is she after you?

610
00:32:45,600 --> 00:32:47,520
Of course not! Sylvia is not like that.

611
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:50,080
It's hard to say, she's a witch!

612
00:32:50,200 --> 00:32:51,640
She's capable of anything.

613
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:53,400
When you pulled out of the investment,

614
00:32:53,560 --> 00:32:55,080
she turned against you right away.

615
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:57,040
She's just jealous.

616
00:32:57,160 --> 00:32:59,480
She thought I'm not yet over Angie.

617
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:01,560
I handled the situation poorly.

618
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:03,600
No wonder she's angry with me.

619
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:06,000
You may know her face, but not her heart.

620
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:09,480
Why else would so many people
point out her problems?

621
00:33:09,600 --> 00:33:11,840
Sylvia is obviously under
intentional attack.

622
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:13,800
Why would there be so many anti-fans

623
00:33:13,960 --> 00:33:15,400
and they are very organized.

624
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:19,560
The damaging information does not
need any substantiation.

625
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:24,080
Angie!

626
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:26,120
Auntie!

627
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:30,440
Here's the power of attorney.

628
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:32,360
Thank you, Auntie.

629
00:33:32,520 --> 00:33:34,440
Thank goodness for you,

630
00:33:34,600 --> 00:33:37,760
or else that witch would have
swindled the flat.

631
00:33:37,880 --> 00:33:39,800
Davis should know what he's doing.

632
00:33:39,960 --> 00:33:42,440
Maybe he's under pressure at work

633
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:44,160
and he got mixed up.

634
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:46,840
Don't be mad at him. He loves you.

635
00:33:46,960 --> 00:33:50,520
Only you can make him come to his senses.

636
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:53,240
How are things with Sylvia?

637
00:33:53,360 --> 00:33:55,480
They probably broke up.

638
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:58,440
That witch was openly criticized online.

639
00:33:58,600 --> 00:34:00,360
Davis finally saw her for who she was.

640
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:02,040
It seems to have turned into a big deal.

641
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:03,560
I have heard about it too.

642
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:07,960
I didn't realize she would con money
and use black magic.

643
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:10,040
She's not to be trifled with.

644
00:34:10,200 --> 00:34:11,640
I checked and found out

645
00:34:11,760 --> 00:34:14,640
she tied Davis' birth data to a gourd.

646
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:17,240
A gourd is supposed to gather wealth.

647
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:18,840
She acted so sweet before.

648
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:20,840
When Davis refused to invest with her,

649
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,880
she turned hostile right away
and went crazy.

650
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,640
But that brat is still not convinced.

651
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:30,280
He planned to talk to her after work.

652
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:32,360
I hope he'll wake up.

653
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:34,360
I took her on before,

654
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:36,520
I knew she's not that simple.

655
00:34:36,640 --> 00:34:38,720
Auntie, you took her on? How?

656
00:34:40,800 --> 00:34:43,880
That time when we first met.

657
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:46,760
Angie, you're so sweet.

658
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:50,280
You're willing to give up the flat
for my son.

659
00:34:50,440 --> 00:34:53,400
Honestly, even I can't do something
so noble.

660
00:34:53,560 --> 00:34:55,120
Auntie, it doesn't matter now.

661
00:34:55,200 --> 00:34:56,440
As long as everything turned out OK.

662
00:34:56,520 --> 00:35:00,080
You asked me to get fertilizer and
sphagnum moss for you.

663
00:35:00,160 --> 00:35:03,000
I bought that and also black diamond soil.

664
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:06,440
That's useful. Take them home later.

665
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:09,720
Angie, you're so thoughtful.

666
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:13,320
It's been a week. Don't be mad anymore.

667
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:15,160
Let's sit down and talk.

668
00:35:15,240 --> 00:35:16,560
I'm on my way over to your studio.

669
00:35:16,640 --> 00:35:18,360
Let's talk about this.

670
00:35:43,320 --> 00:35:46,360
Sylvia, open the door, OK?

671
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:49,880
Let's sit down and talk.

672
00:35:50,760 --> 00:35:52,720
Sylvia?

673
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:58,520
Scumbag, I don't want to see you anymore.

674
00:35:58,640 --> 00:36:00,640
I will not forgive you.

675
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:02,520
I'm returning your things.

676
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:07,080
What you owe me, I won't let it slide.

677
00:36:17,320 --> 00:36:19,160
You're still thinking about her.

678
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,920
What do you mean?

679
00:36:28,960 --> 00:36:30,920
It's not what you think, Sylvia!

680
00:36:52,840 --> 00:36:54,360
What's wrong, Mom?

681
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:55,320
What's going on?

682
00:36:58,440 --> 00:37:00,520
Why so many moths?

683
00:37:04,640 --> 00:37:06,280
It's a bad omen.

684
00:37:09,480 --> 00:37:11,160
Just kidding. Come on...

685
00:37:11,320 --> 00:37:13,960
It's about to rain.

686
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:16,720
Don't mind them. They'll go away later.

687
00:37:16,800 --> 00:37:18,440
Why did you yell?

688
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:20,520
To wake you up.

689
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:22,520
What? You're scared of moths?

690
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:25,240
I'm afraid you're scared of them.

691
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:43,120
(private number)

692
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,720
Sylvia, is that you?

693
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:57,120
Just talk to me.

694
00:37:57,200 --> 00:37:59,960
It's no use playing with the phone.

695
00:38:17,640 --> 00:38:20,280
Mr. Yau, we have a problem with the flat.

696
00:38:20,360 --> 00:38:22,200
This is outrageous!

697
00:38:22,320 --> 00:38:24,280
Look what happened!

698
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:26,360
You told me to clean up the place,

699
00:38:26,480 --> 00:38:28,680
this is what I saw when I opened the door.

700
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:31,960
It's OK. You may go. I'll handle this.

701
00:38:32,040 --> 00:38:32,760
OK.

702
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:46,120
Did you do this? What do you want?

703
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:50,520
Where are you? Let's meet and talk, OK?

704
00:38:58,400 --> 00:38:59,320
Sylvia?

705
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:01,400
I told you I'll make you sorry.

706
00:39:01,560 --> 00:39:03,800
Calm down. Take it easy!

707
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:10,120
Angie?!

708
00:39:12,680 --> 00:39:13,760
(Chan Sin To Memorial Primary School)

709
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:25,240
Angie, where are you?

710
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:27,120
Sylvia, answer me!

711
00:39:27,240 --> 00:39:28,440
Angie!

712
00:39:34,560 --> 00:39:37,000
Angie...Angie, wake up...

713
00:39:39,680 --> 00:39:40,760
Davis...

714
00:39:46,680 --> 00:39:48,200
Don't move...

715
00:39:48,560 --> 00:39:49,560
I'll get you out.

716
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:54,120
Be careful!

717
00:39:54,200 --> 00:39:55,480
Don't worry!

718
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:02,520
Are you OK?

719
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:03,880
I'm OK.

720
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:05,320
Does it hurt anywhere else?

721
00:40:05,480 --> 00:40:06,720
I'm OK.

722
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:10,680
Who brought you here?

723
00:40:11,400 --> 00:40:14,080
I was late getting off work.

724
00:40:14,720 --> 00:40:17,000
On my way home,

725
00:40:17,120 --> 00:40:21,880
I was walking and someone
covered up my face

726
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:23,880
and I passed out.

727
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:25,880
Did you see who it was?

728
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:28,120
No, I didn't.

729
00:40:29,040 --> 00:40:33,800
But I've been harassed lately.

730
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:37,680
(Leave someone else's boyfriend alone,
bloody whore!)

731
00:40:52,840 --> 00:40:56,360
(If you don't let go, I will take action.)

732
00:40:56,840 --> 00:40:59,880
I think it was Sylvia.

733
00:41:00,040 --> 00:41:02,360
I got you into this mess.

734
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:08,920
Why did you stop?

735
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:11,240
Go up and let me dress your wound.

736
00:41:11,320 --> 00:41:14,200
No, I don't want to scare Auntie.

737
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:15,880
Just take me home.

738
00:41:16,760 --> 00:41:18,360
OK, I'll take you home.

739
00:41:38,080 --> 00:41:39,720
I'll walk you up.

740
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:47,160
Think nothing of it.

741
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:50,160
Yau You-fong!
